    "content": "As of early April 2026, over 3.1 million bottles of various eye drops have been voluntarily recalled by K.C. Pharmaceuticals due to potential \"lack of assurance of sterility\". The products, sold at major retailers including CVS, Walgreens, Rite Aid, Walmart, and H-E-B, include various Dry Eye Relief and Artificial Tears products. K.C. Pharmaceuticals What You Need to Do: Stop using the recalled products immediately. Check the FDA recall notice or USAToday for the full list of impacted LOT numbers and National Drug Codes (NDCs). FDA recall notice USAToday Return the product to the store where it was purchased for a refund. Recalled Product Details: Brands Affected: Best Choice, Careone, CVS Health, Equaline, Foster & Thrive, Good Neighbor Pharmacy, H-E-B, Leader, Major, Meijer, QC-Quality Choice, Rite Aid, TopCare Health, and Walgreens. Specific Products: Various sterile lubricant eye drops, dry eye relief drops, and redness relief drops. Expiration Dates: The recall includes products with expiration dates ranging from April 30 to July 31, 2026. Risk: The FDA classified this as a Class II recall, meaning the product could cause temporary or reversible health problems. No injuries or infections have been reported to date. This is a developing situation. Consumers should check for updates on the official FDA website. FDA website",
